  "authorNotes": "Scope: book chapters 6-13 only. The Mohammadpur 2026 Class 3 Maths final is a genuine Class 3 annual paper (/100) but its layout differs from the Sylhet syllabus (no MCQ, no data/pictograph question, no time problem), so its items were spread across the matching Sylhet rows: short answers 1(k,g,chh,jh,nyo) kept in row 3, 1(kh,chh)/3(kh) turned into MCQs, unit conversions 3(k,g,gh) used as row-2 blanks, Q2 computations (125÷5, 18÷6×7, 15×5÷3, money + and −) used in row 4, the Q4 multiplication facts used as row 5 unchanged, Q6(gh) mangoes extended to an 8-mark row 6, Q5(1) fraction picture + Q6(g) distance used for row 7, and Q7 (angle definition, draw angles, rectangle/square definitions — exactly 8 marks) used for row 9. Dropped MP items: 80×30 and 251×26 and 121×4 (chapter 5 multiplication, outside the Sylhet scope), the house-picture question (row 9 is already full with Q7), and the Q6(kha) 4 taka × 365 days problem. Rows 8 (measurement & time creative) and 10 (table & pictograph) had no Mohammadpur match and are new from the book. Row 2 uses only the fill-in-the-blank format (digest: pick one format). Doubts for the owner: (1) Row 9's label says 'চাঁদার ব্যবহার' (using a protractor), but the Class 3 book never teaches the protractor or degrees (it only appears once as an MCQ option, p.147); I left protractor use out and removed it from the printed instruction — please confirm. (2) Row 5 'নামতা লেখ' is set as 10 single multiplication facts (as Mohammadpur did), not as one full table; switch to 'এর নামতা লেখ' with splitMarks if the owner prefers a full table. (3) Duration '৩ ঘণ্টা' copied from Mohammadpur's /100 paper — Sylhet's duration not stated in the syllabus. (4) Row 7 picture: the Office must redraw Mohammadpur's picture (rectangle in 8 equal parts with 4 shaded; circle in 4 equal parts with 2 shaded). All answers were computed and checked twice."
